# public-boundary allowlist — pinned SHA-256 grandfather list.
# Generated by tools/check-public-boundary.py --seed. Every entry represents a
# private surface still tracked in the public repo, pending migration to
# darklanes. Changing a file makes its (path, sha256) tuple miss the list, so
# the check fails and forces a review — either update the hash intentionally
# or migrate the file. The extraction plan lives in
# research/public-boundary-20260814/PROGRESS.md.
#
# `rules` is the SCOPE of the exemption and is required (2026-08-19). An entry grandfathers
# only the rules it names; the same bytes matching any other rule — including a rule added
# later — is a fresh violation. Before that, keying on (path, sha256) alone meant one
# grandfather covered every rule, and a recon journal pinned for `production_endpoint` also
# carried a provider capacity-block id that no report could ever name.
#
# `unremediated` lists rules on an entry that pin a finding NOBODY HAS RULED ON YET. It is not
# an acceptance. The check prints the outstanding count on every run, pass or fail, because the
# two ways to hold an undecided finding are both bad alone: a red gate gets bypassed, and a
# silently pinned one goes quiet. Clearing an entry means remediating the file or the owner
# deciding to keep it and dropping the field — never editing the field alone.
